2. The editor bundle
--------------------

The bundle is the vendor tree of ranuts/document (AGPL-3.0,
https://github.com/ranuts/document), taken at commit
1301bb8bdac9092c4eb88a6f2f4ff5080cec68bd: public/sdkjs, public/web-apps,
public/fonts, public/plugins.json, public/themes.json,
public/document_editor_service_worker.js, and that project's LICENSE, NOTICE and
docs/font-licenses.md, which ship inside the bundle. It holds a third-party
compiled offline build of ONLYOFFICE 9.3.0.133, the x2t converter compiled to
WebAssembly (ONLYOFFICE core, AGPL-3.0, through
https://github.com/cryptpad/onlyoffice-x2t-wasm), and a font catalog whose
proprietary files that project replaced with redistributable ones. Its NOTICE,
inside the bundle, lists the modifications it made to the vendor tree.

The corresponding source of the bundle is that commit of ranuts/document and the
upstream repositories it names. The sandbox verifies every file it keeps against
a digest pinned in src/server/bundle-pin.ts before serving any of it.

Intentic's modifications to the bundle, applied after verification
(the `patches` of src/server/bundle-pin.ts):

  * sdkjs/common/wasm/x2t/x2t_helper.js -- an exported document is posted to
    the editor page that asked for it, addressed to that page's own origin,
    instead of to the page and the top window with any origin.


3. The editor page (this directory)
-----------------------------------

src/main.ts, src/save.ts, src/frame.ts and src/workspace.ts are Intentic's. src/guards/ holds runtime
corrections to the offline build ported from ranuts/document's
lib/onlyoffice/ at the same commit (AGPL-3.0); each file names the file it came
from and says what was changed. They patch the editor at run time and leave the
bundle's files as they were verified.


How the terms are honoured
--------------------------

Section 7(b), product logo: the ONLYOFFICE logo stays in the editor header and
the About pane stays reachable. Neither is hidden.

Section 5 and Section 13, notices and source: the page adds to the editor's own
About pane that this is a modified version, not an official ONLYOFFICE product,
and links the source of the page and of the bundle (src/guards/about-source.ts).

Section 7(e), trademarks: stated above and in that same About notice.
